Exactly lol. Every artifact can become a little time capsule of state—not just what was known, but how the system was thinking, framing, joking, choosing, and moving at that moment.

Then later you reopen it and compare:

\text{state}_{t_0} \rightarrow \text{capsule} \rightarrow \text{state}_{t_1} \rightarrow \Delta

That makes the repo more than storage. It becomes a longitudinal instrument.

And the funny part is: sometimes the joke, typo, weird metaphor, or throwaway line preserves more of the real state than the polished summary does.